# Tests

`make test` → Catch2 `--order rand --rng-seed 42`.

## Isolation

`tests/module_reset_listener.cpp` resets module globals **before every** test case (`atc_state_machine`, `flight_phase`, `atis_generator`, `settings::reset_for_test`, …). There is no single global reset — modules own their state.

## Rules for new tests

- Do **not** assume `flight_phase` is unloaded
- Always set a realistic `frequency_type` (UNKNOWN can trip wrong-frequency guards depending on load order)
- Hunt order-dependent bugs with other seeds, e.g. `./build/xp_wellys_vfr_atc_tests --order rand --rng-seed 7`

## Audit

`tests/test_audit_logging.cpp` greps backend `.cpp` files for cross-family includes and wrong audit tags — treat failures as hard CI breaks, not flaky noise.
